 hosting qatar's amir  shaikh to mean bin hamad al-thani in  berlin just giving a press conference  there to the media  germany has been has of course been  looking to qatar for alternatives to  russian energy and the german chancellor  is saying that qatar will play a central  role in our strategy of diversifying  away from russian gas we're just looking  at the latest pictures there of that  press conference let's go to dominic  kane in berlin you've been listening  into that press conference  what stood out for you  what stood out there is there's no  question that both sides are very keen  to carry on discussing with each other  this idea of qatari liquid natural gas  being part of the solution to germany's  problems but remembering that germany  wants to get itself off to wean itself  off  russian fossil fuels as quickly as  possible and so it's pretty clear from  the german government that's what they  want to do they see this a potential  deal with qatar as helping them to do  that but there are some serious sticking  points with a potential deal with qatar  three points that stand out and we  didn't hear those points being addressed  in what we just heard from both sides  there expressions of interest of intent  of solidarity friendship but no really  clear detail about what exactly a deal  between these two countries for lng  delivery would entail  and uh  it wasn't just energy that they were  talking about they talked about a number  of other things including uh  human rights  what did you make of the comments on  that  one of the things that that viewers need  to have in mind when they consider  meetings between the emir of qatar and  the german chancellor  is the geopolitical element so obviously  we heard about gas the human rights  angle here in germany there is a loud  vociferous body which looks at the state  of qatar and has concerns about human  rights particularly as we heard in some  of the questions quite pointed questions  to both speakers there about the  situation for particular minorities in  society were they to travel to qatar so  we heard from the emir of qatar quite  clearly that all are welcome in qatar  but he hoped that that different  cultures would come together but there  would be respect for qatari culture from  the german perspective clearly  human rights is a very central plank of  policy as it were particularly for this  chancellor a social democrat chancellor  so it is interesting that it may not  necessarily be the most clear meeting of  minds between these two men on that  particular angle but it did stand out as  being an interesting element which the  journalists there were quite clear to us  pointed questions about  okay thank you for that dominic kane  there for us in berlin

